X-SOURCE-ID:thedirt
X-SOURCE:The Dirt
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T170000
DTSTAMP:20260915T024045Z
CREATED:20260915T024019Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260915T024045Z
UID:10083218-1791028800-1791046800@thedirt.online
SUMMARY:Birds & Bikes
DESCRIPTION:Axis Gallery is proud to announce Birds & Bikes\, a collaborative art exhibition bringing together regional artists to explore the poetic intersections of avian flight and human motion. Running from October 2 through November 1\, 2026\, the exhibition showcases a dynamic range of works from intricate metal sculptures and imaginative textile art to curated gallery shop goods\, celebrating the beauty of migration alongside the engineering of daily travel. \nThe exhibition features a direct partnership with the City of Sacramento Office of Arts and Culture (OAC) Art in Public Places program and North Natomas Jibe. Birds & Bikes serves as an artistic tie-in to the upcoming Birds and Benches project\, which will install artist-designed public benches across North Natomas Regional Park. \nVisitors are invited to experience the unique ecology and transit identity of the Natomas Basin through a collaborative lens\, discover one-of-a-kind art pieces\, and browse handcrafted items in the East Gallery Pop-Up Shop. \nParticipating artists include Antonia Price\, Sokthea Chan*\, Linda Clark Johnson\, Nathan Coldwater\, Kate Farrall\, Sandy Fong Whetstone\, Cara Gregor*\, Jordin Hinton\, Heather Hogan*\, Maris Kaplan\, Tanya Lieberman\, Elise Mahan*\, Lo’Vonia Parks\, Judy Coates Perez\, Samuel Rose\, Jenna Savage\, Michelle Sharf\, and Alex Williams. (* indicated Axis Member) \nExhibition & Event Schedule\nExhibition Dates: October 2 – November 1\, 2026\nGallery Hours: Fridays – Sundays\, 12:00 PM – 5:00 PM\nOpening Reception: Saturday\, October 10 | 5:00 PM – 8:00 PM\nArtist Talk: Sunday\, October 25 | 12:00 PM – 2:00 PM (Featuring representatives from Sacramento OAC & North Natomas Jibe)\nLocation: Axis Gallery\, Sacramento\, CA \nJoin us at Axis Gallery\, located at 625 S Street in Sacramento’s historic R Street Corridor\, within the Verge Center for the Arts building. The gallery has exhibited innovative contemporary art for over 35 years and continues to serve as a vital space for artists to explore\, connect\, and share work outside the commercial sphere. \nGallery hours: Friday–Sunday\, 12–5 PM
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/birds-bikes/2026-10-03/
LOCATION:Axis Gallery\, 625 S St\, Sacramento\, 95811\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Birds-Bikes.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Axis Gallery":MAILTO:info@axisgallery.org
END:VEVENT
